# AGENTS.md

This file is the canonical agent-facing map for ${PROJECT_NAME}. Keep it short. Put deeper context in the files it points to.

## Start Here

- Read `ARCHITECTURE.md` for the layering contract and dependency rules.
- Use `docs/exec-plans/active/` for any work that needs durable cross-session state.
- Use `docs/validation-guide.md` when present to choose validation checks.
- Use `INBOX.md` as a capture queue only. It is not the execution source of truth.

## Repo Map

- `ARCHITECTURE.md` - architecture rules and layer boundaries
- `docs/exec-plans/active/` - in-flight ExecPlans
- `docs/exec-plans/completed/` - completed ExecPlans
- `docs/design-docs/` - durable design decisions and supporting context
- `docs/product-specs/` - product-facing intent and behavior
- `docs/references/` - vendor docs, schemas, and reference material
- `docs/generated/` - generated artifacts that help agents reason about the system
- `${APP_ROOT_DISPLAY}` - application code root
- `INBOX.md` - capture queue / parking lot

## Working Rules

- Prefer domain-first placement over global horizontal buckets.
- Keep cross-cutting concerns behind explicit providers.
- Enforce invariants mechanically when possible; do not rely on prose alone.
- Verify observable behavior before calling work done.

